        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix nodejs installation logic on Debian-based systems",
        "body": "### Problem\r\nOn Debian-based systems, a package named `pacman` (the arcade game) exists in the official repositories. If a user has it installed, `command -v pacman` succeeds and the script mistakenly treats the system as Arch-based.\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\nRequire both conditions to be true before using the Arch/pacman installation path:\r\n- `pacman` is available, and\r\n- the distro is confirmed as Arch (`is_arch_linux`)\r\n\r\nThis changes the check from `||` to `&&`, preventing false positives on Debian-based systems.\r\n\r\n### Follow-up (optional)\r\nDear maintainers,\r\nIf you agree, I can send a separate PR to add explicit helpers like `is_debian_linux()` and `is_fedora_linux()` and use them to improve distribution detection for `install_node()` and other needed processes.",
